The problem might be related to https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CAMEL-23174

After HDDS-13034 there was a the deletion thread pool executor that was meant to parallelize deletes per store ends up spawning only one thread and scheduling all delete tasks on that single thread regardless of what `numberOfParallelThreadsPerStore` is configured to.

This is because the workerQueue is unbounded and it only spawns a new thread beyond the core pool size, 0 if the queue rejects the task (which is never because it is unbounded).
{code:java}
this.deletionThreadPool = new ThreadPoolExecutor(0, numberOfParallelThreadsPerStore,
interval, unit, new LinkedBlockingDeque<>(Integer.MAX_VALUE));
{code}

FIRST_VALUE and LAST_VALUE are only defined for window aggregates, but can be used without window clause in current main branch.

