h2. Problem

GET /flowexecutions?q=latestFlowExecution returns HTTP 500 when any execution in the result set has ExecutionStatus.$UNKNOWN. The error surfaces as:

{noformat}
RestLiServiceException [HTTP Status:500]:
  ERROR :: /executionStatus :: "$UNKNOWN" is not an enum symbol
{noformat}

A single poisoned record poisons the entire response batch — other valid executions in the same collection are never returned to the caller.

h2. Impact

* Callers polling for flow status receive 500s instead of usable responses
* Service-level SLOs (5xx-based) register violations for what is really a data-quality issue, not a service fault
* Retries don't help because the underlying record remains in the result set

h2. Root cause

{{ExecutionStatus.$UNKNOWN}} is a Pegasus-generated Java-only sentinel used for forward-compatible deserialization of unrecognized enum values. It is NOT declared in {{ExecutionStatus.pdl}}. Valid schema symbols are: COMPILED, PENDING, PENDING_RETRY, PENDING_RESUME, ORCHESTRATED, RUNNING, COMPLETE, FAILED, CANCELLED.

The value can reach {{FlowExecutionResource.convertFlowStatus()}} via two paths:

# {{JobStatusRetriever.getFlowStatusFromJobStatuses}} initializes its {{flowExecutionStatus}} default to {{$UNKNOWN}} (line 259); if no flow-level status event (NA_KEY/NA_KEY) has been persisted for the execution, that default is returned unchanged.
# Schema version skew: a writer running a newer {{ExecutionStatus}} schema writes a value the current reader does not recognize, and the Pegasus deserializer substitutes {{$UNKNOWN}} on read.

When that value reaches the response, {{RestLiValidationFilter}} rejects it during serialization and throws a 500.

h2. Fix

In {{FlowExecutionResource.convertFlowStatus}}, coerce {{$UNKNOWN}} to {{PENDING}} before constructing the {{FlowExecution}} response, and log a WARN so the underlying data-quality issue remains observable:

{code:java}
ExecutionStatus flowExecutionStatus = monitoringFlowStatus.getFlowExecutionStatus();
if (flowExecutionStatus == ExecutionStatus.$UNKNOWN) {
  log.warn("FlowExecution {}/{}/{} has $UNKNOWN flow status; coercing to PENDING. ...",
      ...);
  flowExecutionStatus = ExecutionStatus.PENDING;
}
{code}

{{PENDING}} is chosen because it semantically represents "flow exists, terminal state not yet known" — the least-misleading valid enum value for this case.

h2. Related followup (not in this change)

{{FlowCompilationValidationHelper.java}} already carries a TODO to stop {{$UNKNOWN}} from leaking out of {{getAllFlowStatusesForFlow}} at the source. That internal-path cleanup is worth pursuing as a separate ticket.

