And just to explain the reasoning behind the switch to ESM - this is what AI thinks about it:


Here is why you should switch from CJS to ESM: * *Standardization & Future-Proofing:* ESM is the official ECMAScript standard, whereas CJS is a legacy system designed for Node.js before modules existed in the language.
 * *Performance (Tree-Shaking):* ESM uses static structure ({{{}import{}}}/{{{}export{}}}), allowing bundlers like Webpack or Rollup to perform "tree-shaking"—removing unused code to create smaller, faster bundles. CJS modules are dynamic and harder to optimize.
 * *Asynchronous Loading:* ESM supports asynchronous loading, improving efficiency in both browser and server environments.
 * *Top-Level Await:* ESM allows the use of {{await}} at the top level of modules, simplifying asynchronous initialization code.
 * *Better Interoperability:* Modern Node.js and browser environments are moving toward native ESM support.
 * *Improved Safety:* ESM provides "live bindings," which are more secure and predictable than the mutable exports of CJS.

