Currently, the Calcite CSV adapter (`CsvTableFactory`, etc.) hardcodes the comma (`,`) as the field separator. This prevents users from mapping schemas to other popular delimited format types, such as pipe-separated (`|`) or tab-separated (`\t`) files.
 
This improvement introduces support for a `separator` property in the model JSON's operand map for the CSV adapter.
 
Example Usage:
{
 "version": "1.0",
 "defaultSchema": "TEST",
 "schemas": [
 {
 "name": "TEST",
 "type": "custom",
 "factory": "org.apache.calcite.adapter.file.CsvTableFactory",
 "operand": {
 "file": "data.csv",
 "separator": "|"
 }
 }
 ]
}
 
If no separator is provided in the model JSON, the adapter defaults to the standard comma (`,`) character, strictly preserving backward compatibility.

