The JVM doesn't support adding annotations in the bytecode for statements and expressions. That doesn't mean that Groovy couldn't support source-level AST transforms in those places. Code injection can happen in the normal way, and the transform will be "forgotten" after compilation.

 Examples might be:
{code}
