Here is the code which produces this log messages. Assume there is one failed datanode cannot be connected, in the while loop, every time sis.recoverChunks returns a full strip data(not sure if exactly one strip, but likely far less than block size), failedIndexes is not null, this logBlockGroupDetails will be called once, so hundreds of duplicated message are created during one block reconstruction. 


{code:java}

