The optimizer is failing to use an available index when a query contains multiple, redundant range predicates on the same indexed column. The optimizer should be able to simplify the redundant predicates and utilize the index for better performance. As an example:
{{}}
{code:java}
drop dataverse test if exists;
create dataverse test;
use test; create type d2 AS { id: int};
create dataset d1(d2) primary key id;
create index a on d1(b); 
select * from d1 where b>1 and b>5;{code}
{{ }}
We should use the index on b and use b>5 for the index search.

After upgrading from CXF 4.1.3 with Spring Boot 3 to CXF 4.2.0 with Spring Boot 4, my test on CXF metrics detected that metric 'cxf.server.requests' in Micrometer for JAX RS Server has duplicated value.

I am creating server with below method:
{code:java}
@Bean
Server rsServer(Bus bus, MetricsProvider metricsProvider) {
    JAXRSServerFactoryBean jaxrsServerFactoryBean = new JAXRSServerFactoryBean();
    jaxrsServerFactoryBean.setBus(bus);
    jaxrsServerFactoryBean.setServiceClass(HelloServiceRSImpl.class);
    jaxrsServerFactoryBean.setServiceBeans(Arrays.asList(new HelloServiceRSImpl()));
    jaxrsServerFactoryBean.setAddress("/");
    jaxrsServerFactoryBean.setFeatures(Arrays.asList(new MetricsFeature(metricsProvider)));
    return jaxrsServerFactoryBean.create();
